# AI context exclusions.
#
# Patterns follow gitignore syntax. Tools that respect this file (Continue,
# Cursor via .cursorignore symlink, custom agent harnesses) will skip these
# paths when building context. `.gitignore` covers build output and runtime
# junk; this file covers TRACKED files that AI agents shouldn't need.
#
# Re-measure after changes:
#   git ls-files | grep -vFf <(grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)' .aiignore | sed 's:^/::; s:/$::') | xargs wc -c | tail -1

# ── Already-tracked binaries (variable fonts, logos, raster images) ─────────
# 1.4M tokens of SVG brand logos; agents working on the API don't need them.
docs/platforms/logos/

# Variable fonts: text-tokenizable but pure noise.
**/*.ttf
**/*.otf
**/*.woff
**/*.woff2

# Raster + vector images outside the logo dir.
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.ico
**/*.webp
**/*.pdf

# ── Generated artifacts regen-able from source ──────────────────────────────
# openapi.yaml is the canonical generated spec; json is the same content in
# a different serialization. Keep yaml in context, drop json.
docs/openapi/openapi.json
docs/openapi/platform-slugs.json

# Postman collection is derived from openapi.yaml.
docs/postman/

# Platforms catalog is regenerated from each vertical's PLATFORMS metadata.
docs/platforms/platforms.json
docs/platforms/platforms.md

# Api-reference markdown is regenerated from openapi.yaml.
docs/api-reference/api-reference.md

# Built docs-server search index.
apps/docs-server/dist/

# ── Lockfiles ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# ── Snapshot/fixture trees the agent rarely needs in full ───────────────────
# Uncomment if your agent runs hit token limits; these are legitimate but
# bulky. Leave commented so they stay in context by default.
# **/__snapshots__/
# docs/integrate/
